  "answer": "The assistant should not treat the sales note's \"immediately on request\" claim as the governing commitment. The official Security and Data Governance Policy is the sole authority for deletion timelines, and standard deletion occurs within 90 days after contract termination [NL-007#NL-007-S06]. Upon contract termination, data is removed from active user access and TutorChat queries immediately, but physical deletion from primary storage and backups can take up to 90 days [NL-019#NL-019-S05].\n\nThe sales playbook also instructs sales reps not to promise immediate deletion without consulting the Security and Governance Lead, and any custom data-decommissioning agreement must go through formal legal review [NL-009#NL-009-S08]. Faster deletion is possible only through a negotiated Enterprise exception documented in a signed Data Processing Agreement, such as a 30-day active purge and 60-day backup purge [NL-007#NL-007-S06]. Verbal or informal sales assurances about immediate deletion are not binding and conflict with official policy [NL-023#NL-023-S05].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
